","source_image_checked":false,"scope":"Current complete stem, choices and independent worked solution; attached source images checked where required","repair":{"stem":"An apartment''s selling price is directly proportional to its area. If 127 m² sells for USD 168,275, what is the price of 156 m²?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"USD 237,900"},{"key":"B","text":"USD 208,500"},{"key":"C","text":"USD 136,993"},{"key":"D","text":"USD 206,700"}],"explanation":"Price per square meter is 168,275/127 = USD 1,325. Thus 156 × 1,325 = USD 206,700. The ratio 206,700/168,275 equals 156/127."},"q_digest":"75ea04bf68e0745eb3d1f8118224e298","key_digest":"6b60f2f73431fa7633e80e0648d04539","fingerprint":"4f669fd8862a8d0a718025f9cc6a32c9"},{"id":"132a8052-5811-5b69-8502-b3834dff6527","status":"mathematically_verified","solution":"3(a+2)²−(a+2)+4=3a²+11a+14; D.","expected_key":"D","source_image_checked":false,"scope":"Current complete stem, choices and independent worked solution; attached source images checked where required","repair":{},"q_digest":"c177b3d26a159799a84d66b1bf65512e","key_digest":"aee31bc265d88259d4f2bcd14c262040","fingerprint":"f41b2843df1633dec88f82848982ba14"},{"id":"136b6118-43cb-5ed6-9a08-ba00d0363108","status":"repair_and_verified","solution":"Atmost40 =>h+v≤40;atleast10 =>h≥10;budget800 =>5h+3v≤800; C. Source checked includes800.","expected_key":"C","source_image_checked":true,"scope":"Current complete stem, choices and independent worked solution; attached source images checked where required","repair":{"stem":"In a board game, horizontal moves cost 5 points and vertical moves cost 3 points. Sarah has 800 points left. She may make at most 40 moves in total, including at least 10 horizontal moves. If h and v are her horizontal and vertical move counts, which system represents these conditions? The move counts are nonnegative integers.","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"h + v ≥ 40; h ≤ 10; 5h + 3v ≤ 800"},{"key":"B","text":"h + v ≤ 40; h ≥ 10; h/5 + v/3 ≤ 800"},{"key"